think r1, r2, r3 landed and pushed both remotes. The closing rung carries the reader onto a REAL on-disk Cord record carrying a genuine two-phase transfer a keeper can open and walk, proving the honored recipient is true to the bytes — the mirror of purse_true carried from a per-account double-spend to a two-phase pledge.
think Designed the fixture scene for awk-honesty: genesis 200 to Alice; Alice pledges 100 to Bob at round 1 (id 0x01); Alice posts it at round 2 (honored, Bob receives the reserved hundred); Alice pledges 100 to Carol at round 3 (id 0x02, open). The single post unambiguously honors the round-1 pledge before the round-3 pledge is even seated, and every pledge is affordable, so the app's full commit tie-break and the awk's file-order pledge-state accounting name the same honored recipient.
think The awk reads the phase from the signed body hex: a kind-2 body's first byte is the phase tag (50=P pledge, 48=H post, 56=V void), the id is hex chars 3..34, the pledge recipient hex chars 35..98. It seats open pledges by id, honors on a post (naming the recipient), releases on a void, and prints the triple honored-recipient-hex posted open. The app resolves the record through pledge, finds the first posted pledge's `to`, and reports the identical triple.
obs GREEN first pass on both selftest and app==awk. The triple is Bob (55154f42…) posted 1 open 1 — app and awk byte-for-byte. Selftest also proves the honored pledge's coins reached Bob, the open pledge still holds 100 reserved, conservation of balance + reserved to 200 over the real bytes, and a tampered header refuses BadFormat. Fixture reproducible (generator re-emits byte-identical bytes). Witness GREEN (the Pledge re-runs its green binary at the door), TAME bans clean, width-check exit 0.
loom witness=mycelium_pledge_true_witness result=GREEN triple=55154f42…_1_1 posted=1 open=1 conserved=200 reproducible=true app_eq_awk=true
